AlignMode.description:
What the build does when the two inputs of a node differ in group delay.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::AlignMode;
assert_eq!(AlignMode::default(), AlignMode::Auto);
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&AlignMode::None)?, "\"none\"");
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

BackendSpec.description:
A backend preference of a node: `{"prefer": name}` or `{"require": name}`.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::BackendSpec;
let b: BackendSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"require":"simd"}"#)?;
assert_eq!(b.require.as_deref(), Some("simd"));
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

DropPolicy.description:
What happens when an output is full.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::DropPolicy;
assert_eq!(DropPolicy::default(), DropPolicy::Error);
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&DropPolicy::DropOldest)?, "\"drop_oldest\"");
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

EdgeSpec.description:
A connection from an input or node to a node or output.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::{EdgeSpec, PortName};
let e: EdgeSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"from":"rf","to":"tune"}"#)?;
assert_eq!((e.from.as_str(), e.to.as_str()), ("rf", "tune"));
assert_eq!(e.port, None);
let e: EdgeSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"from":"pilot","to":"pll","port":"b"}"#)?;
assert_eq!(e.port, Some(PortName::B));
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

FormatSpec.description:
A raw sample format in the model: a name (`"cu8"`) or a [`CustomFormat`].

```
use sdrk_pipeline::FormatSpec;
let f: FormatSpec = serde_json::from_str("\"cs16\"")?;
assert_eq!(f.to_format().unwrap(), sdrk_device::formats::CS16);
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

GroupSpec.description:
A node group: the unit that a later runner maps to a thread, a core, a GPU queue or a
remote machine. In this version groups only partition the model.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::GroupSpec;
let g: GroupSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"description":"DDC on core 0"}"#)?;
assert!(g.description.is_some());
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

InputSpec.description:
An input of the pipeline: raw bytes in a `format`, converted samples of a `type`, or
packets (`"type": "packets"`).

```
use sdrk_pipeline::InputSpec;
let i: InputSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"format":"cu8","rate_hz":2400000}"#)?;
assert_eq!(i.rate_hz.map(|r| r.0.num()), Some(2_400_000));
// A packet input that only feeds port `b` of a clocked encoder needs no rate.
let p: InputSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"type":"packets"}"#)?;
assert_eq!(p.rate_hz, None);
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

InputType.description:
The type of an input that delivers already converted samples, or packets.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::InputType;
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&InputType::Packets)?, "\"packets\"");
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

OutputSpec.description:
An output of the pipeline.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::{DropPolicy, OutputSpec};
let o: OutputSpec = serde_json::from_str(r#"{"type":"frames","queue":2}"#)?;
assert_eq!(o.drop_policy(), DropPolicy::Error);
assert_eq!(o.queue_frames(), 2);
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

PortName.description:
The input port of a node that an edge feeds: `a` (the default) or `b`.

A node of a one-input kind has the port `a` only; the two-input kinds (`add`, `mul`,
`make_complex`, `stereo_pll`) need one edge per port.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::PortName;
assert_eq!(PortName::B.as_str(), "b");
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&PortName::A)?, "\"a\"");
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

Precision.description:
Numeric precision of the whole pipeline.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::Precision;
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&Precision::Q15)?, "\"q15\"");
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

Settings.description:
The `settings` object.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::{Precision, Settings};
let s: Settings = serde_json::from_str("{}")?;
assert_eq!((s.precision, s.max_chunk), (Precision::F32, 4096));
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

UnderrunPolicy.description:
What `pull` does when the source has no more data.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::UnderrunPolicy;
assert_eq!(serde_json::to_string(&UnderrunPolicy::Zeros)?, "\"zeros\"");
# Ok::<(), serde_json::Error>(())
```

description:
A complete pipeline description.

```
use sdrk_pipeline::PipelineSpec;
let json = r#"{
  "sdrk": 1,
  "name": "tone",
  "settings": { "precision": "f32", "max_chunk": 4096 },
  "inputs": { "iq": { "type": "c32", "rate_hz": 48000 } },
  "nodes": { "gain": { "kind": "scale", "params": { "gain_db": -6 } } },
  "edges": [ { "from": "iq", "to": "gain" }, { "from": "gain", "to": "out" } ],
  "outputs": { "out": { "type": "stream" } }
}"#;
let spec = PipelineSpec::from_json(json)?;
assert_eq!(spec.nodes.len(), 1);
assert_eq!(PipelineSpec::from_json(&spec.to_json())?, spec);
# Ok::<(), sdrk_pipeline::Error>(())
```
